I’ve settled the v1 semantics: Condition emits exactly one typed branch value; inactive branches propagate `skipped`; Merge is the only tolerant join and runs after every predecessor resolves, consuming only active inputs in saved-edge order. Set Value replaces any optional input with configured JSON, Wait passes JSON through with cooperative delay, and Story Generator emits the existing `script` type. I’m recording that contract before touching runtime code, as step 5.4 requires.
